RESPOND inside TRY sends its response: CATCH doesn't catch it, the code after
END TRY doesn't run, and FINALLY does (Requirement 6.7, 7.4). FINALLY counts
its runs in a module-level map that a second route reads.

### nothing has run yet
GET /cleanups
=> 200

{"cleanups": 0}

### RESPOND inside TRY
GET /haunt
=> 202

{"status": "HAUNTING"}

### FINALLY ran once
GET /cleanups
=> 200

{"cleanups": 1}

### again
GET /haunt
=> 202

{"status": "HAUNTING"}

### FINALLY ran twice
GET /cleanups
=> 200

{"cleanups": 2}
